        },
        "spacer_ykeVbb": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fVaWkq": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How long do your bulk tea lights burn?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_xVMDY7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Our bulk tea light selection includes 4.5-hour, 6-hour, and 8-hour options. That makes it easier to choose the right candle for shorter dinners, standard evening service, or longer events that need more coverage.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_68L9WH": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_63Jihh": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How do I choose between an aluminum cup and a clear cup tea lights?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_dttHE3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose aluminum cup tea lights when you want a practical, high-volume option for service use, lanterns, or less-visible holders. Choose clear cup tea lights when the cup will be seen through glass or water, and you want the finished display to look cleaner and more refined.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_7QXgMW": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_TCpCmP": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which tea light burn time is best for restaurants and hotels?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_zpDMyy": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Longer-burning tea lights are usually the best choice for restaurants and hotels because they reduce the need for mid-service replacement. If the candle needs to last through a full dinner service or event window, a 6-hour or 8-hour option is usually the better fit.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_arXGAk": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fzkidB": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What pack sizes do you offer for bulk tea lights?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_cwjTHJ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We offer a range of bulk pack sizes so customers can choose the quantity that matches the job. That includes smaller bulk formats for testing or lighter use and larger packs for venues, restaurants, planners, and repeat buyers.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_qB4n73": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_zyLdDY": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are your bulk tea lights unscented?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_N7NKXg": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes. Our bulk tea lights are a strong choice for customers who want candlelight without added fragrance. Unscented tea lights are especially useful around dining service, wedding tables, spas, and shared guest spaces.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_iyVR4q": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_8mUwN8": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are your tea lights made for clean burning?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_rFAG4b": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes. Our tea lights are made for clean, consistent performance when they are used in appropriate holders. That makes them a practical option for events and hospitality settings where dependable burn quality and easier cleanup matter.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_MErJfP": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fqn9Nh": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Can I use bulk tea lights outdoors?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_kfetKV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, but they should be protected from the wind. Tea lights perform best in lanterns, hurricane holders, or enclosed glass so the flame stays steady and the setup remains safe and visually clean.<br/><br/></p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_4rYLVA": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_RYkkeN": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Who usually buys bulk tea lights from Kisco Candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_7mgpPx": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Our bulk tea lights are a strong fit for event planners, restaurants, hotels, spas, venues, and customers who use candles regularly. They are especially useful when you need a compact candle format that is easy to place in larger numbers.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_pUXFBb": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_hAVpBc": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "When should I choose tea lights instead of floating candles or pillars?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_JyT4aY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose tea lights when you want low-profile accent lighting that does not take up much space. They are usually the better choice for cocktail tables, side tables, restrooms, lounge areas, and smaller decorative moments where a larger candle would feel oversized.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        }
      },
